  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper introduces a hybrid qGAN for approximate quantum state preparation of probability distributions, demonstrated with 3-qubit circuits (depth k≤3) trained on 20,000 samples. Training is validated via Kolmogorov–Smirnov statistics and relative entropy, including a hardware run on IBM Q Boeblingen. The trained generator is used in a simulated Quantum Amplitude Estimation example for European option pricing, using 8 evaluation qubits and showing comparable confidence intervals to Monte Carlo while using 256 vs 1024 samples.",
